WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.707
This is Level 2 of the Prompt Studio, on the free plan.

00:00:03.707 --> 00:00:05.571
In Level 1 you followed a recipe.

00:00:05.571 --> 00:00:10.260
Here you write your own: define a scenario, craft the prompt, check it, then build.

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:17.221
On the free plan, usage refills over a few hours, and open ended prompting uses it fastest.

00:00:17.221 --> 00:00:21.570
So plan before you prompt, keep builds small, and download every version.

00:00:23.067 --> 00:00:25.282
The scenario canvas has twelve parts.

00:00:25.282 --> 00:00:30.610
Each one has a coaching question, examples you can reveal, and live feedback as you type.

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:31.987
Green means it's clear.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:33.834
Stuck?

00:00:33.834 --> 00:00:36.169
Copy the interview prompt into a new chat.

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:39.672
Claude asks you questions one at a time, then writes a summary.

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:42.230
Paste the summary here, and press Fill canvas.

00:00:44.167 --> 00:00:48.355
Choose a design system, then pick the device, fidelity and output format.

00:00:48.355 --> 00:00:52.487
Tick Ready for Desktop Tester if you'll test your prototype in that app.

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:55.877
Press Assemble prompt.

00:00:55.877 --> 00:01:00.800
Your canvas becomes a full prompt in the workspace, and it's yours to edit however you like.

00:01:02.333 --> 00:01:05.683
The quality gate scores your prompt out of ten as you edit.

00:01:05.683 --> 00:01:08.237
Aim for eight before you send a build prompt.

00:01:08.237 --> 00:01:09.883
Then copy it into a new chat.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:15.812
For follow ups, use the prompt patterns, such as three variants or a scope fence.

00:01:15.812 --> 00:01:19.353
And check Fake it honestly for anything that would need a server.

00:01:19.353 --> 00:01:20.170
That's Level 2.
